 <longdesc><para unique="1261255">Performs a bitwise logical AND of inverted second operand (the first source operand) with the third operand (the second source operand). The result is stored in the first operand (destination operand).</para>
  <para unique="1261256">This instruction is not supported in real mode and virtual-8086 mode. The operand size is always 32 bits if not in 64-bit mode. In 64-bit mode operand size 64 requires VEX.W1. VEX.W1 is ignored in non-64-bit modes. An attempt to execute this instruction with VEX.L not equal to 0 will cause #UD.</para>
  </longdesc>
 <operation>
  <programlisting>DEST := (NOT SRC1) bitwiseAND SRC2;
SF := DEST[OperandSize -1];
ZF := (DEST = 0);</programlisting>
  </operation>
 <subsection title="Flags Affected">
  <para unique="1261262">SF and ZF are updated based on result. OF and CF flags are cleared. AF and PF flags are undefined.</para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Intel C/C++ Compiler Intrinsic Equivalent">
  <programlisting>Auto-generated from high-level language.</programlisting>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="SIMD Floating-Point Exceptions">
  <para unique="1261266">None.</para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Other Exceptions">
  <para unique="1261271" format="xIndent1">See <link unique="1261269" linkend="&lt;c&gt;__sdm_vol2A_ch02.fm#59669: 06_Table: Table 2-30. Exception Definition (VEX-Encoded GPR Instructions)" xrefstyle="Table All - no page-period">Table&#160;2&#8209;29, &#8220;Type 13 Class Exception Conditions.&#8221;</link></para>
  </subsection>
 </instruction>
